<title>FRENCH GUIANA: Ariane rocket launches PanAmSat satellite.</title>
<headline>Ariane rocket launches PanAmSat satellite.</headline>
<dateline>KOUROU, French Guiana 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Europe's 98th Ariane rocket blasted off from French Guiana early on Friday and placed into orbit a communications satellite for global satellite operator PanAmSat.</p>
<p>The Ariane-4 rocket lifted off at 3.46 a.m local time (0646 GMT). Twenty-one minutes after takeoff, the PanAmSat-6 satellite separated from the rocket, space officials said.</p>
<p>The 3.4-tonne satellite will provide direct television broadcast services to South America. It was built in the U.S. by Space Systems/Loral.</p>
<p>Friday's mission was the 27th consecutive successful launch of an Ariane-4 rocket.</p>
